-- title:
--   Supersingular component chart at q=2 with q+1 nodes
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(k_A, M')$ over the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace` and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$. Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the first being the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, the second the function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$). Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(k_A,M')$ — a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and degree-preserving on places — subject to the Gauss-type compatibility that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and has residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally let $s \in W$. Then there are a field $FSS$ that is an algebra over $k_A$, a component chart $C$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ along $A$ with reduced field $FSS$, and a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $k_A$, such that: $FSS$ contains an element transcendental over $k_A$; for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which has non-negative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $C.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $C$-residue is the image in $FSS$ of the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$; for every $q$-th primitive root of unity index $\zeta$ and every $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, the pullback of $C$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ has the same ring of integers as $C$; $\#N = q+1$; and for every place $Q$ of $FSS$ over $k_A$ with $Q \notin N$ there is $T \in C.\mathrm{integers}$ with $C$-residue nonzero of order $1$ at $Q$, such that every $P \in C.\mathrm{dom}$ with $C.\mathrm{placeMap}\,P = Q$ has $T$ in its valuation subring with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,T$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, and for every $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ there is exactly one $P \in C.\mathrm{dom}$ with $C.\mathrm{placeMap}\,P = Q$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,T = c$; moreover every such $P$ gives non-negative order to the image of $j$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$.
--
--   This is the local description of the supersingular tube of the full-level modular curve at the residue characteristic $q=2$, under the rigidifying assumption that the auxiliary level $M'$ is divisible by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$: a component chart over a supersingular place $s$, stable under the level automorphisms, with $q+1$ distinguished places and an open-disc fibre free of cusps over each remaining place. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
